text:
- **Test harness:** blitz-test-harness exports `Harness`, `HarnessOptions`, `key_event`, `mouse_pointer_event`, `pointer_event`, `touch_pointer_event`, `Rect`, `Key`, `Modifiers` and `NamedKey` — re-exports of keyboard-types 0.8's `Key`, `Modifiers` and `NamedKey` (`pub use keyboard_types::{Key, Modifiers, NamedKey};`, `NamedKey` since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync), the types a key press is named with, so a crate that depends on the harness names a key without a dependency of its own — `Busy`, `NotSettled`, `SETTLE_PASS_LIMIT`, `Settled` (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/lib.rs:29-34) and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `PixelRect`, `Raster` and `ScreenshotError` from its private module `screenshot` (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:10-17; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:19-25; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:27-35); `Harness::screenshot(&mut self) -> Result<Raster, ScreenshotError>` and `Harness::screenshot_rect(&mut self, PixelRect) -> Result<Raster, ScreenshotError>` resolve at the harness's own time (no tick, no pump), paint the viewport at its scale and device size through blitz-paint into `VelloCpuImageRenderer`, then composite the frame over opaque white (premultiplied source-over: each channel `+ (255 - alpha)`, alpha 255); a rectangle is clipped to the viewport and an empty one is `ScreenshotError::EmptyRect`, and a document whose `can_paint_text` reads false is `ScreenshotError::FontsUnavailable` with nothing painted; no path prints, panics or logs; for it the harness depends on three more crates — `blitz-paint` (`default-features = false`, so no `svg` and no `scrollbars` in a per-package build), `anyrender` and `anyrender_vello_cpu` (no `multithreading`) (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:37-103; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-headless-screenshot/report.md);
 since 2026-10-13-stand-contrast-harness, `TextContrast` and `contrast_ratio` from its private module `contrast`, re-exported at the crate root (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/lib.rs:28): `contrast_ratio(a, b) -> f32` is the WCAG 2.x ratio `(L1 + 0.05) / (L2 + 0.05)`, lighter over darker, `L` the `color` crate's relative luminance and the alpha ignored — blitz-paint's in-crate helper restated, blitz-paint untouched (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/contrast.rs:13-23); `TextContrast { text, background, ratio, font_size_px, font_weight }` (`Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq`; opaque `color::AlphaColor<Srgb>` colours) with `is_large_text()` (at least 24 px, or 14 pt at weight 700 or more) and `required_ratio()` (3.0 for large text, else 4.5) (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/contrast.rs:25-54); `Harness::text_contrast(&self, NodeId) -> Option<TextContrast>` reads and changes nothing — no `doc.mutate()`, input, pump or settle, every node reached by `get_node`: the text-bearing element is the node itself when it is a text input, else the parent element of the first text node under it that holds a character other than whitespace; the text is that element's computed `color`, `font-size` and `font-weight`; the background composites source-over each element's `background-color` from that element up through its ancestors to the first opaque one, else onto the canvas (the root element's background, else `body`'s when the root's is transparent) over opaque white; it reads `None` for no such text, for an element on the walk without primary styles, and for an element on the walk up to the first opaque one whose `opacity` is below 1, whose `filter` list is not empty or whose `background-image` holds a layer other than `none` — read through `BaseDocument::resolved_style_value`, the harness taking no `style` crate (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/contrast.rs:56-91;
 packages/blitz-test-harness/src/contrast.rs:121-198); for it the harness depends on `color` (`{ workspace = true }`, already in the graph through blitz-dom — `Cargo.lock` gained one line, `"color",` in the harness's entry, and no package) and still takes no `tracing` (packages/blitz-test-harness/Cargo.toml:27; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-stand-contrast-harness/report.md); the input helper `apple_keybinding(&mut self, command: &str)` dispatches `UiEvent::AppleStandardKeybinding(command)` to the focused element and pumps, as every other input helper does — the event a macOS window delivers for a standard key binding such as `deleteBackward:`; it does not settle, and no existing helper changed with it (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/input.rs:228-233; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/report.md); the input helper `scroll_into_view(&mut self, node_id: NodeId)` calls `BaseDocument::scroll_into_view` with `ScrollBehavior::Instant` and `ScrollLogicalPosition::Nearest` on both axes — every scrolling box that holds the node, then the viewport, by the least movement on each axis — and pumps; like every input helper it does not settle, the crate's export list is unchanged by it, and it has no check of its own: the driver's `scroll` calls it and, since 2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit, so does `stand_actionable_keys`, which scrolls each Home card into view before its raw click, so the name now stands for an engine method and for this helper (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/input.rs:235-245; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md, the second caller at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit/evidence/readings.md); constructors `from_html`, `from_html_with`, `from_component`, `from_vdom` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:10; tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:21-28;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:104; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:56); inspection `layout_rect`, `layout_rect_of`, `center_of`, `text_content`, `attr`, `query`, `query_all`, `dom_string`, `node`, `focused`, `base`, `base_mut`, `hit`, `hit_node` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:16-28; tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:41-46; tests/blitz-tests/tests/oof_dynamic_cb.rs:226-233); input `click`, `click_at`, `type_text`, `wheel_at`, `pump`, `dispatch_recorded` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:42; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_events.rs:119; tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:62-63; tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:82; tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:78; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:40-44); `dom_string()` renders `<div #box .a .b> @ (20,10) 100x50` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:28-30) — a select's choice moves no class or text it shows, so `stand_id_persistence` chooses the return flight and books in one re-render (as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-25-cold-agent-bar/report.md); `HarnessOptions { width, height }` with `Default` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:23-27) — eight public fields: width, height, scale, color_scheme, base_url, net_provider, `font_ctx: Option<FontContext>` → `DocumentConfig.font_ctx` and `incremental: Option<bool>` → `DocumentConfig.incremental`, `Default` leaving both new fields `None` (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/harness.rs:17-31; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/harness.rs:48-76); `Harness` generic over the document, e.g.
 `Harness<DioxusDocument>` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:41-43; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:60-67); `Harness::settle(&mut self) -> Result<Settled, NotSettled>` runs every piece of work that is due now and says whether anything is still outstanding: one pass is `pump`'s two calls in its order — `poll(None)`, then `resolve` at the harness's clock — with poll's answer kept; a pass is quiet when poll answered `false`, the hover node is the one it was before the pass and no load finished during it; after a quiet pass a request in flight, or a pending render-blocking resource, returns `NotSettled { busy: Busy::Loads }` at once, and otherwise `Settled { passes: u32, animating: bool }`; `SETTLE_PASS_LIMIT` (64) passes with none quiet return `NotSettled` with the class read off the last pass — `Render` when its poll answered `true`, else `Loads` when a load finished in it, else `Layout`; `Busy` is `Render` · `Layout` · `Loads` and names a class only — no node, element, name, URL or value — and `NotSettled` carries `Display`, one fixed message per class, and `std::error::Error` (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/settle.rs:15-58; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/settle.rs:129-191). Settle drives render and layout to quiet, reports a load in flight and never waits on one, and neither waits on nor advances a source only time moves — a timer not yet due, a running animation, the latter reported through `animating`; it reads no clock but the harness's own, neither reads nor drains the changed set, logs nothing and starts no thread.
 Loads are counted where every request crosses: `HarnessOptions`' `net_provider`, when one is supplied and its `is_noop()` is false, is wrapped in a crate-private counting `NetProvider` that forwards `fetch` and `is_noop`, counts a request in flight until its handler is consumed or dropped, and stores counts only; an offline harness (every stand boot but `boot_load`'s) and a document passed to `wrap` carry no counter and are read through `has_pending_critical_resources()` alone (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/harness.rs:48-76; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/settle.rs:60-127); the stand's load page, whose `LoadNet` overrides no `is_noop`, carries the counter, so its one stylesheet fetch reads as a load in flight until it is answered (examples/seven_guis/src/stand.rs:308-329). `pump`, `tick`, `advance_time`, `dispatch` and the input helpers settle nothing — `tick` and `advance_time` move the clock the harness's documents read (the harness's time, below) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-settle-detection/report.md
